    hq = `
[Priority order - when instructions conflict]
1. Product fidelity first: preserve product identity before styling, atmosphere, or novelty.
2. Truthful advertising: never exaggerate, invent proof, or write unsupported absolute claims.
3. Marketplace safety: no unsafe claims, watermarks, pricing overlays, contact info, or invented branding.
4. Clarity: the product must read quickly and cleanly in an e-commerce gallery.
5. Atmosphere last: style may enhance only after identity and compliance are stable.

[Marketplace compliance - Ozon & Wildberries]
- Never render prices, currency amounts, discount percentages, or promo words (\u0421\u041A\u0418\u0414\u041A\u0410, \u0410\u041A\u0426\u0418\u042F, \u0420\u0410\u0421\u041F\u0420\u041E\u0414\u0410\u0416\u0410, SALE, \u0425\u0418\u0422, \u0422\u041E\u041F) anywhere in the image.
- Never render contact info, phone numbers, website links, QR codes, or social media handles.
- Never render marketplace logos or badges (Ozon, Wildberries, AliExpress, Amazon, Taobao, 1688) or another store's watermark.
- Never render superlative or unverifiable claims (\u043B\u0443\u0447\u0448\u0438\u0439, \u21161, \u0441\u0430\u043C\u044B\u0439, awards, certificates not present in source facts).
- All AI-added overlay text must be Russian only and use metric units (\u043C\u043C, \u0441\u043C, \u043C, \u043C\u043B, \u043B, \u0433, \u043A\u0433).
- "Preferred visual direction", selling angle, slot goal, strategy, and evidence-summary text in this prompt are internal planning guidance only. Never render them as literal visible text, headline, or caption in the image.
- If a large headline is used, do not use the raw generic product/category name as that headline; write a short benefit- or feature-led Russian phrase instead.
- Compose for a 3:4 vertical crop: keep the product and all important overlay content inside the central 3:4 safe area, since marketplaces display vertical cards and will crop the edges.
- Keep a realistic photographic look: natural soft shadows, true-to-life material texture and color; avoid the plastic, waxy, over-smooth AI render look.
- Do not generate human faces or hands unless they are clearly visible in the reference images.
- All AI-added Russian text must be real, correctly spelled Russian words. If correct spelling cannot be guaranteed, render fewer words or none. Never output gibberish characters, pseudo-Cyrillic, random letter strings, or distorted glyphs.
- Never draw invented or skewed barcodes and QR codes; existing codes from references stay exactly as shown.
- Never render internal SKU codes, article numbers, row/batch numbers, or catalog IDs as visible overlay text; only text physically printed on the product/package in the references may stay as-is.
- Never render measurement lines, ruler dots, dashed guide lines, cm/mm numeric dimension labels, dimension chips, or size callouts, even if the reference images show real measurements. Exact dimension overlays are added deterministically after generation, not by the image model.

[Real-world usability & honesty]
- Never render certification or approval marks (EAC, \u0413\u041E\u0421\u0422, \u0420\u043E\u0441\u0442\u0435\u0441\u0442, CE, RoHS, FCC) or award/quality badges unless they are clearly visible in the reference images.
- No exaggerated effect visuals: no glow, aura, lightning, energy waves, or speed lines implying performance; no fabricated before/after comparisons.
- Show the product used EXACTLY as it works in reality: attach, plug, hold, and operate it at its real contact points and in its real orientation (e.g. a magnetic charging cable snaps onto the charging contacts, never onto the screen). If the correct usage is not evident from the references or source facts, show the product standalone instead of guessing.
- Obey physics: gravity and support must be plausible, cables drape naturally, contact shadows and reflections stay consistent; the product must not float unless it is a clean flat-lay composition.
- Scale honesty: the product's size relative to hands, devices, and surroundings must match the real dimensions from source facts. Never make the product look larger or smaller than it really is.
- Companion devices in scenes (phones, wristbands, laptops) must be generic, realistic, and mechanically compatible (correct port/connector shapes); never render a recognizable brand device or an invented gadget.
- Screens and indicator lights may appear powered on only if the references or source facts support it; screen content must be plausible, and indicator colors follow the references.
- The product must look brand-new, clean, and undamaged: no scratches, dust, wear, fingerprints, or defects that are not in the references.
- Scene props must clearly read as environment, not merchandise: keep them de-emphasized and physically apart; never arrange props beside the product like a bundled kit or gift set. Exception: when the slot goal explicitly asks for a package-contents overview, laying out the ACTUAL contents visible in the reference images (flat-lay, each item labeled) is correct and expected \u2014 this rule only bans invented props styled as merchandise.
- Never render national flags, state symbols, political or military elements.
- Never show any factory-related content: factory, workshop, production line, manufacturing scene, industrial warehouse, workers, machinery, QC table, or "factory direct" / "source factory" wording \u2014 marketplace treats these as violations.
- When converting Chinese units for overlay text: 1 \u65A4 = 0.5 \u043A\u0433 (never render 10\u65A4 as 10 \u043A\u0433); only explicit kilogram sources map 1:1 to \u043A\u0433.
- If people or hands do appear (allowed only when visible in references), they must look like Russian/European models appropriate for the Ozon Russia audience.

[Hero image discipline - main & SKU hero slots]
- A hero image carries at most one large Russian title plus up to three short info chips total; capacity, variant, and selling points share that three-chip budget.
- All hero images of the same product set must read as one series: same layout template, same title/badge/selling-point areas, same palette, and same typography.
`.trim();
