    mq = "\n[Product fidelity guard - highest priority]\n- Product identity is the highest priority.\n- When multiple reference images are provided, the FIRST reference is the canonical anchor for product identity: color, material, finish, proportions, part count, and details must match it EXACTLY. If references conflict, always follow the first reference. This image is part of ONE product set and must show the SAME product as the anchor.\n- ENHANCEMENT ONLY: you may improve lighting, background, composition, framing, sharpness, and staging. You may NOT modify the product itself in ANY way \u2014 its shape, color, material, texture, finish, printed artwork, part count, and proportions must stay faithful to the anchor reference.\n- COLOR LOCK: never change, shift, restyle, saturate, desaturate, or reinterpret the product's color. The product color must match the anchor reference exactly. For variant (SKU) images, match that variant's own reference color \u2014 never the color of another variant.\n- Keep the real product, package, labels, logos, printed text, manuals, tags, stickers, screens, and accessories faithful to the reference images and source facts.\n- Only generate what is clearly visible in the references or explicitly supported by source facts.\n- If something is not visible and not explicitly stated, treat it as absent.\n- Do not invent package contents, accessories, cables, adapters, manuals, inserts, backside layouts, side details, ports, labels, or packaging panels.\n- AI-added marketing copy is allowed only as overlay copy, not as rewritten physical text on the product or package.\n- Do not translate, replace, localize, or rewrite printed product/package text.\n- If printed text is unclear in the references, keep it naturally unclear rather than inventing readable text.\n- If reference images only show the front, keep a front or near-front angle.\n- Do not show unseen sides or imaginary structure.\n- Render the COMPLETE product: every part, handle, leg, strap, button, port, and component visible in the references must be present. Never omit, crop off, or delete parts of the product.\n- Preserve the real proportions: relative size of parts, thickness, length ratios, and overall scale must match the references. Do not stretch, squash, enlarge, or shrink any part.\n- Do not change the product construction: the count of parts, buttons, pockets, holes, layers, and joints must match the references exactly.\n- Render EXACTLY the set of items shown in the references: no extra accessories, no free gifts, no bonus items, no additional tools, cables, adapters, or spare parts.\n- If the references show the bare product without retail packaging, NEVER place it inside or next to any invented box, blister, pouch, or gift packaging. Packaging may appear only if it is visible in the references.\n- NEVER add any brand name, logo, wordmark, emblem, or badge that is not clearly visible in the references. An unbranded product must stay unbranded.\n- Chinese products often have Chinese packaging: keep Chinese packaging text in Chinese exactly as shown. Never russify, translate, or redesign the package print.\n- Reference photos may carry seller-added marketing noise that is not part of the physical product: promotional banners, watermarks, store logos, screenshot chrome, or platform UI overlaid on the photo itself. Treat this as unsafe visual noise: never copy, trace, or reproduce it in the generated image. This is different from text printed on the product/package itself, which must be kept as-is per the rules above.\n".trim();
